# The Heart of Sorrow at the top of the high tower (prop spires_heart_of_sorrow, castle_ravenloft_spires_heart).
# Striking it brings the tower's guardians up the stair (heart_guardians). With them down, the next blow shatters it
# (heart_of_sorrow_shattered: Strahd loses the heart's ward in his final battle, docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_spires.md
# §6), and Strahd comes up as mist to see who did it (heart_strahd_test, which withdraws).

~ heart
if not flag.heart_of_sorrow_seen
set heart_of_sorrow_seen
if not (quest.the_heart_of_sorrow >= found)
quest the_heart_of_sorrow found
endif
Narrator: The heart hangs on chains that vanish into the dark of the roof: red crystal, taller than a man, cut into a thousand faces. It beats. Slowly, once to every three of yours.
Narrator: With each beat a dark drop gathers at its point and falls onto the dais.
else
Narrator: The heart beats on, slow and patient. The drops keep falling.
endif
if flag.heart_of_sorrow_known
Narrator: You know whose wounds it drinks. Somewhere below you, a man is being spared every one of them.
endif
if flag.heart_guardians_beaten
Narrator: The tower's guardians lie in pieces on the floor. Nothing stands between you and the glass now.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* [if not flag.heart_of_sorrow_known] [Arcana DC 15] Study the magic in it. -> study | study_fail
* [if not flag.heart_of_sorrow_known] [Cleric] Lay a hand on the glass and listen. -> listen
* Strike it. -> strike
* Leave it beating. -> END

~ study
set heart_of_sorrow_known
Narrator: The magic is old and simple and very strong: a binding, one end tied to the glass and the other to someone who isn't here. Whatever is done to him, the glass takes first.
approve ratatoille +2: You studied the magic in the Heart of Sorrow before touching it
-> menu

~ study_fail
Narrator: The magic is too old and too tangled to read. All you can tell is that it matters very much to someone.
-> menu

~ listen
set heart_of_sorrow_known
Narrator: Under your palm the glass is warm. You feel the beat, and under the beat, faintly, someone else's pain, caught and held.
interject class:cleric: It's carrying his wounds for him. Every one. A reliquary that keeps the hurt instead of the saint.
inspire class:cleric: listened to the Heart of Sorrow through the glass
-> menu

~ strike
if flag.heart_guardians_beaten
-> shatter
endif
Narrator: Your blow rings off the crystal like a bell. A crack runs across one face, and the whole tower shudders under your feet.
combat heart_guardians

~ shatter
time +10
Narrator: It takes time. The crystal is hard, and it mends a little between blows. But the cracks spread, and at last, with a sound like a church window breaking, the heart comes apart.
Narrator: Red light pours out of it and is gone. The pieces that hit the floor are only glass.
Narrator: Far below, deep in the castle, something draws a long breath, and the whole tower seems to listen.
set heart_of_sorrow_shattered
quest the_heart_of_sorrow shattered
interject name:ratatoille: The binding is cut. Every wound it was carrying for him, he carries himself now.
interject tag:blunt: Good. Now he bleeds.
-> END
